    "title": "Aaron Boone Comments on Dodgers' Behavior After World Series Victory",
    "text": "• Aaron Boone is the manager of the New York Yankees.\n• Boone spoke with journalists on October 26, 2024, before Game 2 of the World Series.\n• He expressed hope that the Yankees would win a championship like the Dodgers did the previous season.\n• Boone criticized some Dodgers players for their comments about the Yankees during the offseason.\n• He stated, 'I don’t like listening to that,' regarding the Dodgers' remarks.\n• Boone acknowledged that the Dodgers had the right to speak after winning the series.\n• The Yankees lost the 2024 World Series to the Dodgers, who won in five games.\n• The Dodgers won Games 1 and 2 at Dodger Stadium and Games 3 and 4 at Yankee Stadium.\n• In Game 5, the Dodgers capitalized on multiple errors by the Yankees to win 7-6.\n• Boone referred to the Dodgers as a 'great team' and 'great organization.'\n• After the World Series, Dodgers relief pitcher Joe Kelly made comments about the Yankees' performance.\n• Kelly described the Yankees' play as 'careless' and suggested they were a lower-tier playoff team.\n• Dodgers player Chris Taylor used profanity to describe the Yankees' Game 5 collapse.\n• Boone noted that the biggest stars of the Dodgers did not disrespect the Yankees.",
